a=[('A-WATER','Water envelope','1,000,000 m3/year gross use: 840,000 new freshwater plus 200,000 internally reclaimed water; not an awarded abstraction right. 40,000 m3/year upstream distribution loss; 800,000 fresh reaches uses.','No water right, quality, treatment or supply alignment supplied. Gross use and reclaimed transfer must not be added as independent sources. Construction waits for lawful reliable supply.'),('A-PILOT','Existing pilot accounting','600,000 m3/year of agriculture envelope provisionally reserved for existing pilot; owner metering must replace this before operation. No fixed arrays, plants or grazing arrangements changed.','Actual existing annual use is not supplied; this is a placeholder allowance, not a measurement. A higher verified pilot requirement reduces all new discretionary allocation before changing the pilot.'),('A-RATES','Domestic and new agriculture','2,400 residents at 160 L/person/day = 140,160 m3/year; new irrigation 170,000 m3/year; panel washing 8,263.2 m3/year. Total agriculture including pilot 778,263.2 m3/year.','Conservative design assumptions including community facilities; crop trial irrigated area capped at 30 ha plus nursery, not all reserved agricultural land irrigated.'),('A-COOL','Cooling basis','Average IT 9 MW (12 MW for 12 hours, 6 MW for 12 hours); annual IT 78,840 MWh. PUE 1.25; site WUE 0.02 L/kWh; annual compute water 1,576.8 m3.','Closed-loop chip cooling with dry heat rejection and air-cooled mechanical trim; WUE includes makeup and facility uses, no evaporative tower. Performance targets require supplier confirmation at 44 C.'),('A-ENERGY','Hourly energy scenario','40 MW PV; synthetic annual capacity factor 25%; 480 MWh battery, 75 MW converter, 95% efficiency each direction; 216 MWh delivered reserve held for 72 hours at 3 MW critical load. Grid import capacity assumed 30 MW; no export.','Illustrative 8760-hour sinusoidal profile, 22% seasonal variation and three dust days each 60 days. No site weather series, tariff or connection offer supplied. tools/energy.py is reproducible, not validated forecasting.'),('A-RETURN','Reuse mass balance','200,000 m3/year treated reuse: 100,000 domestic return + 50,000 industrial return + 50,000 captured agricultural drainage; dispatched 180,000 agriculture and 20,000 landscape. Of annual 840,000 fresh input, 40,000 is distribution loss and 800,000 terminal consumption/losses.','Separate grey and black water treatment, filtration, disinfection and salinity checks required. No condensate or stormwater yield credited. No uncontrolled brine disposal; salt concentrates go to contained handling and licensed removal.'),('A-SHORT','30 percent gross-use reduction','From 1,000,000 to 700,000 m3/year: landscape 20,000 cut; new irrigation and washing 178,263.2 cut; industry 40,000 cut; domestic/community nonessential use 61,736.8 cut. Existing pilot 600,000 and compute makeup 1,576.8 protected.','Gross-use shortage specified by brief, distinct from fresh-water shortage. Domestic/community residual is 78,423.2 m3/year (89.52 L/person/day including communal uses), an emergency assumption requiring verified essential-use sufficiency; if insufficient, secure emergency import or defer occupancy rather than deprive essential use.'),('A-FLOOD','Screening buffers','Permanent structures excluded from DEM flood band plus 30 m and from channel centrelines plus 150 m; reserve uses flood band plus 150 m. No design flood discharge claimed.','DEM channels omit small washes and external northern catchments. These offsets are assumed screening distances, not flood protection standards; 2D hydraulic study and ground survey required.'),('A-SEISMIC','Structural concept','One to three storeys; regular reinforced concrete frames and ductile walls, braced light roofs; conceptual separation gaps 100 mm minimum subject to drift calculation; design reference INPRES-CIRSOC 103 Part I 2018 with applicable addenda to be confirmed by local engineer.','No soil class, spectra or geotechnical report supplied. Geometry is urban design, not structural certification.'),('A-ACCESS','Access allowance','80 km assumed external RN40 road corridor, 8 m carriageway and nominal 20 m reservation; 640,000 m2 pavement allowance outside site plus the drawn internal network. Eastern RP510 option held for later.','RN40 is 27.6 km from the nearest site edge, not this settlement. Actual external route and length unresolved. Schematic avoids claiming off-site rights; comparative alignment, easements, flood crossings and capital funding are phase-one prerequisites.'),('A-SHADE','Heat and light','Shade share counts actual proposed roof coverage; thermal comfort requires testing. 2200 K shielded night lighting; no facade uplighting; 10 lux route design target subject to engineering.','No outdoor comfort simulation or illuminance survey available. Enclosed cooled refuges are required at 44 C; shade is not a guarantee of safe conditions.'),('A-HOUSING','Population and employment','960 dwellings; 2.5 persons per dwelling = 2,400 residents; 1,200 local jobs. 1,080 resident workers, 120 inbound specialists; 120 resident remote workers, 600 children/students, 300 retired adults, 300 unpaid carers or job-seekers.','Programme targets, not labour-market estimates. Resident categories sum to 2,400; remote-worker income, pensions and household transfers support nonlocal-job households.'),('A-HEAT','Heat receivers','Drying cooperative accepts annual 3,942 MWh usable heat, equal to 5% of IT electricity, via a metered insulated loop and temperature-lift heat pump if required.','Declared contracted-use target; herb drying and process wash-water preheat are named receivers, not assumed continuous demand. Reject all unused heat to air; no winter greenhouse demand invented.'),('A-GROWTH','Growth ceiling','Three settlements and a 7,200-resident long-term ceiling, conditional on independently demonstrated incremental water and complete services; stage 2 cumulative 2,400 jobs, stage 3 cumulative 3,600 jobs.','A deliberately modest ceiling, not a population forecast. Reservations confer no development entitlement.'),('A-COST','Funding order','Infrastructure escrow and 12 months public-service operating reserve precede dwelling occupation; compute concession pays annual fixed community service charge independent of runtime.','No prices or financing terms supplied; these are proposed enforceable contract conditions, not existing agreements.')]
basis_notes={'A-WATER': 'No supplied water right or supply design. Reuse is an internal transfer. Construction requires lawful reliable fresh supply.', 'A-PILOT': 'Existing use is unmetered here. Higher verified demand reduces new discretionary uses first; existing operations remain unchanged.', 'A-RATES': 'Assumed rates, not local measurements. New irrigation is capped at 30 ha plus nursery; reserved farmland is not all irrigated.', 'A-RETURN': 'Assumed recoverable returns require treatment, disinfection and salinity checks. No rain or condensate yield credited. Concentrates require contained handling and licensed removal.', 'A-ACCESS': 'Actual route, easements and crossings unresolved. The nearest-site distance is not the settlement access length. Phase one requires funded access.', 'A-FLOOD': 'Screening offsets, not hydraulic standards. Minor washes and external inflows are missing; ground survey and 2D modelling required.'}
write('assumptions.json',{'assumptions':[dict(id=i,topic=t,value=v,basis=basis_notes.get(i,b)) for i,t,v,b in a]})
